<h2><span style=3D"color: rgb(255, 0, 0);">Vote by Mail "Opt-Out"</span></h=
2>
<p><em>Voters can notify their county clerk or registrar that they do not w=
ant to receive a mail ballot if they prefer to only vote in-person. This pr=
ocess to "opt-out" of receiving a mail ballot must be done not later than 6=
0 days before Election Day. The "opt-out" deadline before the primary elect=
ion is&nbsp;<strong>April 10, 2026</strong>. The "opt-out" deadline before =
the general election is&nbsp;<strong>September 4, 2026</strong>. To "opt-ou=
t", voters may either print and submit a paper form to their clerk or regis=
trar or submit the request online using the links below. *Using the online =
method will automatically submit the form to your county clerk or registrar=
.<br>
</em></p>
<p>To access the&nbsp;<strong>opt-out</strong>&nbsp;form for the 2026 elect=
ion, please click here:<a tabindex=3D"-1" href=3D"https://www.nvsos.gov/hom=
e/showpublisheddocument?id=3D9827" target=3D"_blank">&nbsp;</a>[<a href=3D"=
https://www.nvsos.gov/home/showpublisheddocument/19437/639161667260100000" =
target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener" tabindex=3D"-1">English</a>], [<a href=
=3D"https://www.nvsos.gov/home/showpublisheddocument/19439/6391616682322700=
00" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener">Spanish</a>], or [<a href=3D"https:/=
/www.nvsos.gov/home/showpublisheddocument/19421/639161636187700000" target=
=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener">Tagalog</a>].</p>
